{
  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a high peak (e.g., >85) followed by a drop, the model consistently underestimates the immediate rebound and overestimates the subsequent decline; apply a positive correction of +2 to +4 points for the first 3-5 days post-drop.",
    "The model exhibits severe mean reversion bias when sentiment is near zero (0.00), failing to capture high-volatility spikes that occur regardless of sentiment direction; increase forecast volatility by 15% during low-sentiment periods.",
    "When the last 3 days show a downward trend with sentiment < 0.20, the model's linear extrapolation is too smooth and misses sharp V-shaped recoveries; apply an upward correction to the first half of the 30-day horizon.",
    "The model systematically underestimates the magnitude of price spikes (e.g., 85+) that occur after a period of consolidation; increase forecasted peak values by approximately 4-6 points when historical volatility is high but sentiment remains neutral."
  ]
}
